      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1097",
      "html": "<ul><li>Scientific name: Trachelyopterus insignis (Steindachner, 1878)</li><li>Common name: Flag Woodcat</li><li>Size: 200 mm (7.9\") SL</li><li>Etymology: Trachelyopterus, from the Greek trachelos, meaning neck, and pteron, meaning fin; in reference to the long cranial shield, which gives the appearance that the dorsal fin originates at the neck region.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1097",
      "html": "<p>South America: Lower Magdalena River basin. Colombia Caribbean Rivers, Magdalena, Lower Magdalena. Type locality: Río Magdalena, Colombia. IUCN Red List category: Least Concern (last assessed 2014).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1097",
      "html": "<ul><li>pH: 6.2 - 7.2</li><li>Temperature: 23.0-28.0°C (73.4-82.4°F)</li><li>dH 10-25</li></ul><p>Note: Fishbase lists 23-38°C - the latter is most likely a typo.</p>"
    },
